oll a ten you get to reroll?[/quote]<br /> <br /> And what do you mean yes? If I take a time penalty I can reduce the difficulty of some disicplines?<br /> Where is this mentioned?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-27-2020, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25749-thealmightykue","name":"TheAlmightyKue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:32:44-07:00","id":1399457,"title":"","content":"<br /> 1. Yes. Which means that there's no reason NOT to specialize if you're min/maxing. Say, take Occult &quot;Vampires&quot; then you get to roll an extra die for every ten when asking about vampire subjects.<br /> <br /> 2. In this case, just Vicissitude because it's a crafting power. The idea being the Tzimisce can horribly mutilate a prisoner over the course of months and correct any mistakes they make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:35:09-07:00","id":1399458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399450-v20-a-few-questions?p=1399457#post1399457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Yes. Which means that there's no reason NOT to specialize if you're min/maxing. Say, take Occult &quot;Vampires&quot; then you get to roll an extra die for every ten when asking about vampire subjects.<br /> <br /> 2. In this case, just Vicissitude because it's a crafting power. The idea being the Tzimisce can horribly mutilate a prisoner over the course of months and correct any mistakes they make.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Where is the crafting power thing mentioned? is it in the v20 core book? Got a page number?<br /> <br /> \u200bIs there anywhere that gives guidelines and rules for the crafting system in v20? I have looked through every thing associated with crafting in the core rulebook and not a thing shows up. No rules for how long crafting the item would take, if I have the proper materials on hand. As far as I can see you roll a set a die and it just magically poof into your hand.<br /> <br /> Like I saw the bit about Malleable Visage for decreasing the difficulty for taking longer. But I can't find any mention of a time frame for crafting. Its just not anywhere near crafting or the system section of the core book, so where would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25749,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25749-thealmightykue","user":"TheAlmightyKue","date":".  Adding more questions. 06-27-2020, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25749-thealmightykue","name":"TheAlmightyKue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T10:02:29-07:00","id":1400337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheAlmightyKue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399450-v20-a-few-questions?p=1399458#post1399458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Where is the crafting power thing mentioned? is it in the v20 core book? Got a page number?<br /> <br /> \u200bIs there anywhere that gives guidelines and rules for the crafting system in v20? I have looked through every thing associated with crafting in the core rulebook and not a thing shows up. No rules for how long crafting the item would take, if I have the proper materials on hand. As far as I can see you roll a set a die and it just magically poof into your hand.<br /> <br /> Like I saw the bit about Malleable Visage for decreasing the difficulty for taking longer. But I can't find any mention of a time frame for crafting. Its just not anywhere near crafting or the system section of the core book, so where would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, the basics.<br /> <br /> V20 rules don't tend to break out situations for individual treatment. That is, there won't be sections titled: &quot;Repairing a Device&quot;, &quot;Searching for Secret Doors&quot;, and &quot;Jumping Across a Gap&quot;. Instead, the rules (p245-266) give a general mechanic which can be applied to nearly any situation.<br /> <br /> Usually, like 99% of the time, you add an attribute+an ability. The storyteller and players decide the exact pool to be used.<br /> <br /> Crafting items, per se, is used as an example on p263. Notice there are multiple options available to players, and difficulty varies based on the complexity of the work. So... there's that. Unfortunately for your original question, it doesn't really apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not the best format, sorry.<br /> 1. What is the point of specializations? I mean in your Abilities and Attributes. Is there some benefit for a Tzimisce for example to specialize in body craft over just pumping his medicine up?<br /> 2. I saw somewhere, forgive me I do not remember where, that for things like Malleable Visage you can reduce the difficulty &quot;If you take enough time&quot;<br /> <br /> Things like this always confuse me when I am reading through the websites for bits of information because I come out feeling like I have not a single clue about this game. </div> </div> </div>You see, a more specific rule is used if it's available rather than a less specific rule. That is, for item creation broadly you would use the rules on p263, but since specific rules are provided in the description of Vicissitude on p241, you use those rules. Thus, Vicissitude is not a Crafts roll, it is a Medicine roll.<br /> <br /> 1. In the case of Vicissitude 1, Body Crafts is a helpful thing to have. Whenever a player makes a die roll involving an activity in which her character has specialized, she may count any die that comes up \u201c10\u201d as two successes instead of just one. (see p96) In effect, each die has a 10% chance of yielding two successes. This may not seem like much, but with a large dicepool it comes up often. It is also one of the few ways to get more than 10 successes in a single roll. With Intelligence 5 and Medicine 5, you can get 10 successes max. Add in a specialty, and you could... in theory... get 20 successes. You'd have to roll ten 10s, but it could happen.<br /> <br /> Bottom line, you get a specialty when you reach the fourth dot, anyway. It's nicer to have than not have. When it helps you, yes, it's somewhat helpful. Statistically, it's nothing to write home about, though.<br /> <br /> If the goal is to make Vicissitude 1 easier to use, take the merit Promethean Clay from Lore of the Clans. It makes shapechanging (yourself) a reflexive action, removes the need for physical sculpting, and reduces your difficulty by 2. For example, duplicating a subject is ordinarily difficulty 8, meaning 30% of your dice will be successes. With the merit, that rises to 50% of your dice.<br /> <br /> 2. Taking extra time is... read as written... a little thorny. Vicissitude's description says it takes more time to use the power than most disciplines, especially to make improvements. This implies it might be an extended action (see p251), which would allow you to roll multiple times accruing successes. The description does not, raw, <i>say</i> it is an extended action, which would allow a single roll, but imply a faster process... roughly one of those notoriously variable units of time called a &quot;turn&quot;. So, speak with your ST about how they plan to run it.<br /> <br /> If the point of the extra time is to improve your odds of success, consider other means to improve rolls.<ul><li>Again, I say, take Promethean Clay. (LotC, p238)</li> <li>Willpower is your second best option. (see p267)</li> <li>Teamwork might be effective, if you have a properly designed Retainer. Call him &quot;Igor&quot;! (p253)</li> <li>Some merits (other than Promethean Clay) might apply. Acute Sense and Lucky come to mind. (p479)</li> <li>If you still fail, trying again at a higher difficulty may be an option. (p251)</li> <li>Ask your ST about equipment bonuses, like how weapons give a modifier. For this, use medical equipment or fancy make-up mirrors. (p279)</li> <li>It's a stretch, but ask about bearing modifiers. Cathari for seductive appearance, Metamorphosis for frightening, etc. (p 310)</li> <li>You likely have Auspex. Ask your ST if checking your work as you go along might help.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}